1
00:00:23,481 --> 00:00:24,816
We're taking down the Tokugawa.

2
00:00:34,993 --> 00:00:35,952
An angel…

3
00:00:38,997 --> 00:00:40,290
Am I dreaming?

4
00:00:41,541 --> 00:00:42,459
You're awake.

5
00:00:48,381 --> 00:00:51,384
That's right. I fell…

6
00:00:54,804 --> 00:00:55,847
Was it you who…

7
00:00:56,473 --> 00:00:58,016
Thank him.

8
00:00:58,099 --> 00:00:59,559
Your wounds were severe,

9
00:00:59,642 --> 00:01:03,021
so I stitched them up
and applied mugwort salve.

10
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:07,400
You need at least three days of rest.

11
00:01:09,486 --> 00:01:10,779
I'll leave you some food.

12
00:01:12,989 --> 00:01:15,533
How about I treat you
to tea sometime to thank you?

13
00:01:17,035 --> 00:01:18,912
What happened to your face?

14
00:01:24,959 --> 00:01:27,921
If you don't want to die,
never touch me again.

15
00:01:28,004 --> 00:01:29,214
I can't breathe…

16
00:01:31,174 --> 00:01:35,637
Is Lord Yukimura really serious
about letting him join us?

17
00:01:36,137 --> 00:01:37,347
I'm against it too.

18
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:39,724
He said loyalty can go to hell.

19
00:01:40,475 --> 00:01:42,894
He's more of a thief than a ninja.

20
00:01:45,396 --> 00:01:46,815
A high-stakes gamble.

21
00:01:46,898 --> 00:01:48,650
Fifty-fifty.

22
00:01:48,733 --> 00:01:50,944
Who are you calling a thief, huh?

23
00:01:51,027 --> 00:01:52,695
-You sure talk a lot of trash.
-Hey!

24
00:01:52,779 --> 00:01:55,490
I already told you, I'm not joining you.

25
00:01:55,573 --> 00:01:56,866
You're up already?

26
00:01:56,950 --> 00:02:00,245
Man, I'm starving. Give me more.

27
00:02:00,328 --> 00:02:02,914
-Rice is precious.
-You're not getting any rice!

28
00:02:02,997 --> 00:02:04,040
Cheap bastard!

29
00:02:07,627 --> 00:02:09,420
Thanks for the food, though.

30
00:02:09,504 --> 00:02:11,631
Isa made it. The one over there.

31
00:02:13,716 --> 00:02:14,968
It was you?

32
00:02:15,051 --> 00:02:16,094
Got a problem with that?

33
00:02:17,679 --> 00:02:20,765
Perfect seasoning, perfect rice.

34
00:02:21,516 --> 00:02:22,892
You're a genius!

35
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:26,396
Oh, really? Then try this, too.

36
00:02:26,479 --> 00:02:29,732
It's rare for Brother to like someone.

37
00:02:29,816 --> 00:02:30,900
Damn, that's good!

38
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:33,361
You could make a fortune
opening a restaurant.

39
00:02:33,444 --> 00:02:34,696
-A restaurant?
-Yeah.

40
00:02:35,947 --> 00:02:38,032
Isa's cooking is good, isn't it?

41
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:39,409
It's great.

42
00:02:39,492 --> 00:02:44,455
So, Sasuke, how about
lending us a hand for a while?

43
00:02:45,039 --> 00:02:48,501
We're going to escape this place
and head to Osaka Castle.

44
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:50,587
We need your help.

45
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:51,921
Escape?

46
00:02:52,005 --> 00:02:56,259
The Tokugawa have our lord confined here.

47
00:02:56,342 --> 00:02:57,677
Why Osaka?

48
00:02:57,760 --> 00:03:01,764
To save Lord Hideyori
and his mother, Lady Yodo,

49
00:03:01,848 --> 00:03:03,766
who are resisting Ieyasu.

50
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:08,855
Once we're in Osaka Castle,
we can help you avenge the old man.

51
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:12,567
Of course, you'll be rewarded.

52
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:15,320
How about two gold coins?

53
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:17,030
Two gold coins?

54
00:03:17,113 --> 00:03:19,574
You don't look like
you've got that kind of money.

55
00:03:21,242 --> 00:03:22,619
Don't worry.

56
00:03:22,702 --> 00:03:26,039
Once we're in Osaka Castle,
we should get a hefty advance.

57
00:03:27,624 --> 00:03:28,958
You're not lying, are you?

58
00:03:29,042 --> 00:03:31,836
Our lord defeated the Tokugawa twice.

59
00:03:32,587 --> 00:03:34,380
They'll welcome him with open arms.

60
00:03:37,008 --> 00:03:38,551
Three gold coins.

61
00:03:38,635 --> 00:03:40,136
Don't get too greedy!

62
00:03:40,220 --> 00:03:41,971
Careful about what you say.

63
00:03:42,931 --> 00:03:44,766
You need me, don't you?

64
00:03:46,434 --> 00:03:47,435
All right, then.

65
00:03:49,270 --> 00:03:51,439
I have one more condition.

66
00:03:52,106 --> 00:03:53,024
Let's hear it.

67
00:03:57,278 --> 00:04:00,698
When we get to Osaka,
how about we go eat konpeito together?

68
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:03,368
Enough of your nonsense,
you filthy monkey.

69
00:04:04,077 --> 00:04:05,620
What's got you so riled up?

70
00:04:09,207 --> 00:04:12,710
-Don't tell me you have feelings for her?
-That's not it.

71
00:04:16,422 --> 00:04:18,633
So, what do you want me to do?

72
00:04:19,634 --> 00:04:22,553
-Kill the enemy soldiers?
-You stupid monkey.

73
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:25,473
If it were that simple,
we'd have done it ourselves by now.

74
00:04:26,557 --> 00:04:29,686
First, let me explain Kudoyama Village.

75
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:34,357
The village is surrounded
by rivers and fences,

76
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:37,151
so everyone must pass through
this checkpoint to enter or leave.

77
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:38,820
INNER GATE

78
00:04:38,903 --> 00:04:42,282
The checkpoint
has an inner and an outer gate,

79
00:04:42,365 --> 00:04:45,785
both heavily guarded by Shuto,
the village watchman,

80
00:04:45,868 --> 00:04:48,204
and his men.

81
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:50,873
There are also watchtowers.

82
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:56,129
Each tower has a scout ninja
watching over the entire village.

83
00:04:57,088 --> 00:04:59,841
The checkpoint also has a ninja
who listens for sounds.

84
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:01,884
They're always listening
for anything suspicious,

85
00:05:01,968 --> 00:05:05,138
so the slightest noise
will bring the guards running.

86
00:05:06,222 --> 00:05:08,766
We could just jump the fence like I did.

87
00:05:09,600 --> 00:05:12,854
Only you and Saizo could pull that off.

88
00:05:13,938 --> 00:05:18,026
This entire village is a prison
to keep me confined.

89
00:05:18,109 --> 00:05:21,404
Of course, we've tried to escape
many times over the past 14 years,

90
00:05:21,487 --> 00:05:23,281
but never succeeded.

91
00:05:23,364 --> 00:05:26,409
No wonder,
with a bunch of losers like these.

92
00:05:26,492 --> 00:05:27,869
What do you mean by that?

93
00:05:28,453 --> 00:05:32,332
An old geezer, a dice-rolling old man,
a bespectacled weakling, and…

94
00:05:34,417 --> 00:05:35,418
Who are you?

95
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:38,504
You all look hopeless.

96
00:05:40,673 --> 00:05:42,633
If enemies show up,
I'll take them all out myself.

97
00:05:42,717 --> 00:05:44,844
If they were that easy,
we'd have done it ourselves.

98
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:47,805
We've endured this long
because we couldn't.

99
00:05:47,889 --> 00:05:51,225
-Don't get cocky, weakling.
-Weakling? What?

100
00:05:51,976 --> 00:05:53,478
Then I'll show you.

101
00:05:54,145 --> 00:05:55,480
Watch closely.

102
00:06:00,735 --> 00:06:01,778
Clone.

103
00:06:07,992 --> 00:06:08,910
Clone!

104
00:06:12,205 --> 00:06:15,458
Even Saizo can't use
the advanced Clone technique.

105
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:18,669
-No way you can pull that off.
-I did, I swear!

106
00:06:18,753 --> 00:06:22,090
My lord, he'll only disrupt our unity.

107
00:06:22,965 --> 00:06:24,342
I won't work with a monkey.

108
00:06:24,425 --> 00:06:25,593
Now, now…

109
00:06:25,676 --> 00:06:28,096
He's a flying monkey, at least.

110
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:29,972
Who are you calling a flying monkey?!

111
00:06:30,056 --> 00:06:32,850
Come on, it's good to have someone
with some guts around.

112
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:36,145
Besides, he's just like I was
when I was young.

113
00:06:37,105 --> 00:06:38,231
Don't be ridiculous.

114
00:06:38,314 --> 00:06:40,399
There's no way
I'll turn into an old geezer like you!

115
00:06:42,652 --> 00:06:43,820
So…

116
00:06:43,903 --> 00:06:45,947
How do you plan to get out of the village?

117
00:06:46,489 --> 00:06:47,490
I've got a plan.

118
00:06:48,241 --> 00:06:49,325
Will you help me?

119
00:06:56,249 --> 00:06:57,625
Fine. But you owe me konpeito.

120
00:06:57,708 --> 00:06:58,626
Yuri…

121
00:06:58,709 --> 00:07:00,837
Fine, I'll help you.

122
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:07,510
Lord Yukimura's orders are absolute.
Can you follow them?

123
00:07:08,594 --> 00:07:10,471
I don't like being told what to do.

124
00:07:11,139 --> 00:07:12,890
I'll decide for myself.

125
00:07:14,016 --> 00:07:15,059
Very well.

126
00:07:15,726 --> 00:07:16,769
Saizo.

127
00:07:17,562 --> 00:07:21,607
Head into town
and get us the latest firearms.

128
00:07:21,691 --> 00:07:22,692
Yes, sir.

129
00:07:23,276 --> 00:07:25,236
Firearms? Why?

130
00:07:25,319 --> 00:07:28,030
Ieyasu has ninja
with superhuman abilities,

131
00:07:28,114 --> 00:07:30,491
led by Hattori Hanzo.

132
00:07:31,284 --> 00:07:33,703
We can't beat them in a fair fight.

133
00:07:36,747 --> 00:07:38,666
Hattori Hanzo…

134
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:42,503
I've seen one of them myself.

135
00:07:43,463 --> 00:07:44,464
A ninja named…

136
00:07:46,340 --> 00:07:48,926
Tsuge Kiyohiro.

137
00:07:51,053 --> 00:07:52,847
This was just
after the Battle of Sekigahara,

138
00:07:53,264 --> 00:07:55,600
when we were hiding at a post station.

139
00:08:03,816 --> 00:08:06,986
He was incredibly fast,
and his body was tough.

140
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:11,199
In an instant,

141
00:08:11,282 --> 00:08:12,950
he slaughtered every man there.

142
00:08:13,034 --> 00:08:14,410
TSUGE KIYOHIRO

143
00:08:16,204 --> 00:08:17,747
When I think back to that day,

144
00:08:18,956 --> 00:08:19,790
even now…

145
00:08:22,418 --> 00:08:23,377
Lord Daisuke.

146
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:27,715
The moment you falter,
you've already lost.

147
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:30,718
No matter who the enemy is,
they'll always have a weakness.

148
00:08:30,801 --> 00:08:33,429
Cast aside your fear
and watch them closely.

149
00:08:35,014 --> 00:08:39,810
Everyone here has had their lives
ruined by the Tokugawa.

150
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:43,731
His master was killed.

151
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:46,025
Just like you.

152
00:08:50,988 --> 00:08:52,031
Someone's coming.

153
00:08:54,742 --> 00:08:55,910
Come.

154
00:09:05,836 --> 00:09:07,421
Taking a nap?

155
00:09:09,465 --> 00:09:11,801
Must be nice.

156
00:09:11,884 --> 00:09:13,469
Lord Shuto.

157
00:09:14,011 --> 00:09:16,847
Forgive me for being seen
in such an undignified state.

158
00:09:16,931 --> 00:09:18,182
What's with that?

159
00:09:18,766 --> 00:09:19,850
Pathetic.

160
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:23,145
So, what brings you here?

161
00:09:23,229 --> 00:09:24,355
Last night,

162
00:09:26,148 --> 00:09:29,318
one of the guards claims
he saw a figure flying through the air.

163
00:09:30,611 --> 00:09:31,988
A flying figure?

164
00:09:32,071 --> 00:09:36,117
You haven't secretly taken in any ninja,

165
00:09:37,243 --> 00:09:38,160
have you?

166
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:41,163
Me? Take in a ninja?

167
00:09:42,915 --> 00:09:43,874
Of course not.

168
00:09:44,959 --> 00:09:48,004
What would anyone gain
by serving a man like me?

169
00:09:50,214 --> 00:09:52,842
The village is bustling
with preparations for the festival.

170
00:09:53,593 --> 00:09:57,138
Must've been a startled monkey
jumping around.

171
00:09:59,682 --> 00:10:01,517
If I see anything suspicious,

172
00:10:02,602 --> 00:10:04,645
I'll kill every villager here!

173
00:10:06,188 --> 00:10:07,481
All of you together.

174
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:10,860
You won't be lonely.

175
00:10:12,361 --> 00:10:14,071
-Let's go!
-Yes, sir!

176
00:10:17,658 --> 00:10:21,037
FIREARMS FOR SALE

177
00:10:22,538 --> 00:10:23,789
Are you the foreigners?

178
00:10:25,124 --> 00:10:29,045
The ones who've crossed the sea
from foreign lands?

179
00:10:30,755 --> 00:10:32,423
There's no need to be so wary.

180
00:10:32,506 --> 00:10:33,966
You're welcome here.

181
00:10:36,552 --> 00:10:37,970
Is that a firearm?

182
00:10:43,184 --> 00:10:44,268
Do it.

183
00:10:58,949 --> 00:11:00,034
I have a report.

184
00:11:03,663 --> 00:11:04,664
SUNPU CASTLE

185
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:06,832
Shall we relocate Hideyori,

186
00:11:07,541 --> 00:11:09,960
or demand Lady Yodo as a hostage?

187
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:14,965
After this much humiliation,
surely they'll choose war.

188
00:11:15,549 --> 00:11:17,927
If he attacks someone who hasn't resisted,

189
00:11:18,969 --> 00:11:21,806
it'll tarnish his reputation
as ruler of the realm.

190
00:11:23,599 --> 00:11:28,062
And what of the crackdown
on foreign merchants?

191
00:11:28,646 --> 00:11:32,358
We've secured all the firearms in Japan.

192
00:11:33,818 --> 00:11:34,985
However…

193
00:11:35,069 --> 00:11:36,070
What?

194
00:11:36,153 --> 00:11:37,738
-Hanzo.
-Yes, sir.

195
00:11:38,572 --> 00:11:39,698
Tell His Lordship.

196
00:11:40,908 --> 00:11:44,120
We've received word
that a ninja has entered Kudoyama.

197
00:11:44,662 --> 00:11:46,163
One of Sanada's men?

198
00:11:46,247 --> 00:11:47,581
We don't know yet.

199
00:11:47,665 --> 00:11:48,958
Our two defeats

200
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,877
were both due to ninja.

201
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:56,632
We must never let the Sanada
join forces with them!

202
00:11:57,758 --> 00:11:59,009
Under no circumstances!

203
00:12:04,849 --> 00:12:05,808
I can't see…

204
00:12:11,730 --> 00:12:12,648
Give it to me.

205
00:12:13,774 --> 00:12:14,650
Yes, sir.

206
00:12:18,028 --> 00:12:19,155
ARCHERY MASTER UNNO ROKURO

207
00:12:22,908 --> 00:12:24,994
Curved Shot, Wild God.

208
00:12:29,248 --> 00:12:30,374
Amazing!

209
00:12:30,458 --> 00:12:31,709
The arrow curved.

210
00:12:31,792 --> 00:12:33,752
The ultimate technique
is an arrow that returns.

211
00:12:35,379 --> 00:12:36,505
Let's train.

212
00:12:36,589 --> 00:12:37,590
Yes, sir!

213
00:13:00,279 --> 00:13:01,489
Brother.

214
00:13:02,239 --> 00:13:03,199
You awake?

215
00:13:06,744 --> 00:13:08,954
There's one right here.

216
00:13:10,372 --> 00:13:11,665
Isn't that cheating?

217
00:13:15,044 --> 00:13:17,004
Can I really count on these guys?

218
00:13:31,727 --> 00:13:33,395
Time to eat…

219
00:13:40,069 --> 00:13:41,820
Time to eat!

220
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:49,703
Fine. Come here.

221
00:13:53,874 --> 00:13:54,750
Here.

222
00:13:58,170 --> 00:13:59,046
Here.

223
00:14:01,882 --> 00:14:03,342
Hey! No thanks or anything?

224
00:14:03,425 --> 00:14:04,510
Mom.

225
00:14:05,135 --> 00:14:06,178
I got a rice ball.

226
00:14:06,262 --> 00:14:07,263
What?

227
00:14:15,062 --> 00:14:16,939
Let's eat together, Mom.

228
00:14:17,022 --> 00:14:18,023
Let's eat.

229
00:14:18,107 --> 00:14:19,525
Don't move!

230
00:14:20,943 --> 00:14:22,194
What's that?

231
00:14:23,028 --> 00:14:24,947
Isn't that a ninja tool?

232
00:14:25,030 --> 00:14:26,907
No, it's just a farming tool.

233
00:14:26,991 --> 00:14:28,200
Liar!

234
00:14:29,034 --> 00:14:29,910
Hey.

235
00:14:30,995 --> 00:14:33,038
What the hell is this?

236
00:14:33,122 --> 00:14:34,498
It's obviously a hoe.

237
00:14:36,500 --> 00:14:39,920
No one must know you're here.

238
00:14:40,504 --> 00:14:43,424
And don't leave the house.
Not even a step. Understand?

239
00:14:46,051 --> 00:14:48,345
-Don't mess with me!
-This way.

240
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:50,514
Take that, you ninja!

241
00:14:51,265 --> 00:14:54,143
You ninja!

242
00:14:54,226 --> 00:14:56,812
This way, this way!

243
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:01,191
-See you!
-Thanks.

244
00:15:06,238 --> 00:15:07,907
They saved my butt.

245
00:15:16,248 --> 00:15:18,042
-Oh my!
-Sasuke.

246
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:20,461
Okuni?

247
00:15:23,422 --> 00:15:24,423
What are you doing here?

248
00:15:24,506 --> 00:15:27,676
I'm working
at the village headman's house.

249
00:15:27,760 --> 00:15:29,219
What about you, Sasuke?

250
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,805
Well, let's just say things happened.

251
00:15:33,515 --> 00:15:35,726
Keep it a secret that I'm here, okay?

252
00:15:37,478 --> 00:15:40,189
By the way, Sasuke, so that's your type?

253
00:15:41,857 --> 00:15:43,484
I saw you go, "Oh my!"

254
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:46,695
Actually…

255
00:15:48,614 --> 00:15:50,991
I'm going to eat konpeito
with someone soon.

256
00:15:51,075 --> 00:15:52,618
Oh, really?

257
00:15:54,078 --> 00:15:56,664
What about your promise
to eat dango with me at the teahouse?

258
00:15:59,833 --> 00:16:01,126
Forget it.

259
00:16:04,546 --> 00:16:05,547
Good grief.

260
00:16:08,384 --> 00:16:10,511
I'm quite the heartbreaker, huh?

261
00:16:12,805 --> 00:16:13,806
You sure are.

262
00:16:15,474 --> 00:16:18,310
The sin of breaking a vow is a grave one.

263
00:16:23,107 --> 00:16:24,149
Oh my…

264
00:16:38,288 --> 00:16:40,124
PORT TOWN OF SAKAI

265
00:16:40,207 --> 00:16:41,208
What?

266
00:16:41,291 --> 00:16:43,002
-You don't sell any?
-No.

267
00:16:43,752 --> 00:16:46,714
Lord Tokugawa has bought up
all the firearms.

268
00:16:46,797 --> 00:16:48,882
I doubt you'll find any anywhere.

269
00:16:52,636 --> 00:16:54,388
Why am I stuck coming along, too?

270
00:16:54,471 --> 00:16:58,308
Because you can't sit still.
They told me to take you outside.

271
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:01,562
-I was just out for a walk.
-How many times do I have to tell you?

272
00:17:01,645 --> 00:17:03,897
-If Shuto catches us…
-Yeah, yeah.

273
00:17:05,274 --> 00:17:06,859
By the way…

274
00:17:07,651 --> 00:17:09,737
You look more important than me,
dressed like that.

275
00:17:09,820 --> 00:17:12,781
Who cares about that?
We need those firearms.

276
00:17:13,657 --> 00:17:15,576
We've got to find a way to get them.

277
00:17:19,288 --> 00:17:20,456
The smell of gunpowder…

278
00:17:57,868 --> 00:17:59,036
Stop!

279
00:17:59,787 --> 00:18:00,996
You're pretty good.

280
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:02,790
Drop your weapon, Sasuke.

281
00:18:08,337 --> 00:18:09,630
Forgive me.

282
00:18:09,713 --> 00:18:13,383
This monkey doesn't know how to behave.

283
00:18:17,805 --> 00:18:19,973
A Westerner!

284
00:18:20,057 --> 00:18:21,809
I've never seen one before.

285
00:18:24,520 --> 00:18:26,814
Would you be willing to sell this to us?

286
00:18:29,483 --> 00:18:30,734
Then help us out.

287
00:18:30,901 --> 00:18:32,694
Seems we need firearms
to take down Tokugawa.

288
00:18:32,778 --> 00:18:34,404
Hey! What the hell are you saying?

289
00:18:34,488 --> 00:18:35,739
Who are you?

290
00:18:36,740 --> 00:18:39,326
A ninja from Kudoyama,
beyond those mountains.

291
00:18:40,661 --> 00:18:41,662
A ninja?

292
00:18:41,745 --> 00:18:44,248
You stupid monkey.
Why would you reveal your identity?

293
00:18:44,331 --> 00:18:46,500
Shut up. We have to tell him
if we're asking for help.

294
00:18:47,584 --> 00:18:48,710
Shakespeare said,

295
00:18:49,586 --> 00:18:52,798
"Brevity is the soul of wit."

296
00:18:55,926 --> 00:18:59,054
I've got something I need to do too.

297
00:19:04,476 --> 00:19:08,230
Looks like we'll have to turn
to the underworld.

298
00:19:24,037 --> 00:19:25,080
Something's coming.

299
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:40,220
No way.

300
00:19:45,475 --> 00:19:46,894
Lord Tsuge!

301
00:19:46,977 --> 00:19:47,978
Lord Tsuge!

302
00:19:48,896 --> 00:19:50,689
You arrived sooner than expected.

303
00:19:50,772 --> 00:19:52,274
Where's the Sanada residence?

304
00:19:52,357 --> 00:19:54,610
Yes, sir! Over there.

305
00:19:55,152 --> 00:19:56,320
Tsuge…

306
00:19:56,403 --> 00:19:58,155
Tsuge Kiyohiro.

307
00:20:04,244 --> 00:20:05,913
Are you the master of this house?

308
00:20:08,707 --> 00:20:09,625
I am.

309
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:12,461
I'm Sanada Yukimura.

310
00:20:13,503 --> 00:20:14,880
Where's the ninja?

311
00:20:16,673 --> 00:20:18,091
There are no ninja here.

312
00:20:22,137 --> 00:20:23,513
Something smells off.

313
00:20:24,348 --> 00:20:26,475
I smell a lie.

314
00:20:30,646 --> 00:20:32,814
Lord Tsuge, we've gathered them!

315
00:20:34,358 --> 00:20:36,401
Sanada's ninja.

316
00:20:37,527 --> 00:20:40,614
Answer me, or I'll kill them one by one.

317
00:20:41,198 --> 00:20:42,199
Hey!

318
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:44,034
Where are you?

319
00:20:44,952 --> 00:20:46,078
I know you're here!

320
00:20:50,207 --> 00:20:51,208
Hey!

321
00:20:52,209 --> 00:20:55,045
Hurry up, or these people will die!

322
00:21:12,771 --> 00:21:13,814
Curved Shot,

323
00:21:14,940 --> 00:21:15,941
Wild God.

324
00:21:16,024 --> 00:21:17,401
CURVED SHOT, WILD GOD

325
00:21:25,742 --> 00:21:29,329
Found you.

326
00:21:51,101 --> 00:21:52,060
Unno…

327
00:22:00,652 --> 00:22:01,653
This guy…

328
00:22:02,446 --> 00:22:05,115
He's no ordinary villager, is he?

329
00:22:08,910 --> 00:22:12,414
The six coins he had on him…

330
00:22:13,707 --> 00:22:16,501
That was the Sanada clan's crest, right?

331
00:22:18,879 --> 00:22:20,005
What was it again?

332
00:22:21,298 --> 00:22:23,050
Pay six coins,

333
00:22:23,925 --> 00:22:27,095
and you'll do anything you're told.

334
00:22:28,055 --> 00:22:29,264
Was that it?

335
00:22:31,266 --> 00:22:32,642
He's your ninja, isn't he?

336
00:22:36,146 --> 00:22:37,064
No.

337
00:22:38,857 --> 00:22:39,941
Well, never mind.

338
00:22:40,817 --> 00:22:45,197
Once we're back at the castle,
someone will recognize his face.

339
00:22:47,741 --> 00:22:49,284
If he was one of the ninja

340
00:22:50,285 --> 00:22:53,789
who fought at Ueda 14 years ago,

341
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:56,541
what then?

342
00:23:10,555 --> 00:23:11,848
One of our men

343
00:23:12,682 --> 00:23:14,351
saw a stranger.

344
00:23:16,228 --> 00:23:19,272
He's your ninja, isn't he?

345
00:23:21,483 --> 00:23:22,442
Village headman.

346
00:23:23,443 --> 00:23:25,654
You knew and kept quiet for our sake.

347
00:23:27,030 --> 00:23:28,907
I'm grateful to you.

348
00:23:30,283 --> 00:23:32,661
But I can't keep this a secret…

349
00:23:34,663 --> 00:23:35,664
any longer.

350
00:23:36,331 --> 00:23:38,875
We'll pay for it too!

351
00:23:43,004 --> 00:23:44,256
Please leave!

352
00:23:56,726 --> 00:23:57,936
It's my fault.

353
00:24:01,731 --> 00:24:03,024
All because of me…

354
00:24:06,778 --> 00:24:07,863
Thanks to you,

355
00:24:09,531 --> 00:24:10,866
the villagers were spared.

356
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:20,167
Even if Lord Daisuke hadn't moved,

357
00:24:21,626 --> 00:24:25,005
Unno would still have fired his arrow.

358
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:34,097
Anayama is right.

359
00:24:35,390 --> 00:24:38,226
Without firearms,
we stand no chance against them.

360
00:24:40,228 --> 00:24:42,439
Hope those guys are doing all right.

361
00:24:51,531 --> 00:24:55,035
What the hell are you doing?!
I was wondering where you'd gone.

362
00:24:59,956 --> 00:25:00,832
These guys…

363
00:25:01,666 --> 00:25:02,876
They're Tokugawa ninja.

364
00:25:03,919 --> 00:25:08,590
If a woman needs help,
of course, you help her.

365
00:25:21,895 --> 00:25:23,271
This is awful.

366
00:25:24,231 --> 00:25:25,774
We can't stay in this town anymore.

367
00:25:27,984 --> 00:25:29,819
Mist Concealment.

368
00:25:29,903 --> 00:25:31,404
My apologies.

369
00:25:31,488 --> 00:25:33,031
This is all his fault.

370
00:25:33,114 --> 00:25:35,492
But I thought she was a beautiful blonde.

371
00:25:36,243 --> 00:25:38,703
We have no choice
but to give up on the firearms.

372
00:25:53,260 --> 00:25:54,844
We're running out of time.

373
00:25:55,470 --> 00:25:56,346
Then…

374
00:25:57,931 --> 00:25:58,974
tonight.

375
00:25:59,057 --> 00:26:00,517
Right.

376
00:26:00,892 --> 00:26:02,978
But we need someone who can use a bow.

377
00:26:09,734 --> 00:26:10,694
I can.

378
00:26:10,777 --> 00:26:12,779
Hey, what are you talking about?

379
00:26:12,862 --> 00:26:14,823
We've got old man Unno for that.

380
00:26:25,250 --> 00:26:28,169
So these are the children
Hakuunsai raised.

381
00:26:29,212 --> 00:26:32,048
Yes. They'll make fine ninja.

382
00:26:43,226 --> 00:26:44,894
What spirit!

383
00:26:45,937 --> 00:26:47,355
Well done, well done.

384
00:27:02,912 --> 00:27:04,539
One day,

385
00:27:05,790 --> 00:27:07,917
you'll all become like this man.

386
00:27:09,044 --> 00:27:12,339
And I'll train you, and train you,

387
00:27:13,298 --> 00:27:14,841
and train you until you do.

388
00:27:18,803 --> 00:27:20,847
Tsuge was shot with an arrow in Kudoyama

389
00:27:20,930 --> 00:27:23,266
by a Sanada ninja

390
00:27:24,142 --> 00:27:25,435
disguised as a villager.

391
00:27:26,269 --> 00:27:27,270
Is that so?

392
00:27:43,578 --> 00:27:46,623
Is this indeed the face of one of them?

393
00:27:49,376 --> 00:27:50,335
Hanzo.

394
00:27:51,711 --> 00:27:52,587
Kill them.

395
00:27:54,089 --> 00:27:54,923
Kill them.

396
00:27:56,591 --> 00:27:58,718
Kill them all. Kill them all.
Kill them all.

397
00:27:59,386 --> 00:28:00,220
Kill them.

398
00:28:03,515 --> 00:28:04,808
Not a single…

399
00:28:06,184 --> 00:28:08,645
Sanada ninja is to be left alive.

400
00:28:10,522 --> 00:28:11,439
Understood?

401
00:28:12,899 --> 00:28:13,733
Yes, sir.

402
00:28:14,567 --> 00:28:15,735
GRAVE OF UNNO ROKURO

403
00:28:15,819 --> 00:28:16,945
That guy…

404
00:28:18,238 --> 00:28:19,697
He was incredibly skilled.

405
00:28:21,908 --> 00:28:23,368
Why die in a place like this?

406
00:28:28,289 --> 00:28:29,749
Why die for someone else?

407
00:28:30,959 --> 00:28:32,502
I'll never understand it.

408
00:28:34,879 --> 00:28:36,005
That's fine.

409
00:28:38,049 --> 00:28:41,511
Unno believed in us when he gave his life.

410
00:28:42,971 --> 00:28:45,098
So we'll carry his hopes with us…

411
00:28:47,267 --> 00:28:48,351
and keep living.

412
00:28:52,063 --> 00:28:54,149
Unno told me about you.

413
00:28:55,233 --> 00:28:56,735
He called you the Flying Monkey.

414
00:28:58,611 --> 00:28:59,863
Sarutobi…

415
00:29:00,780 --> 00:29:01,614
Sasuke.

416
00:29:02,657 --> 00:29:04,868
From now on, your name is Sarutobi Sasuke.

417
00:29:05,910 --> 00:29:06,828
What?

418
00:29:07,787 --> 00:29:09,664
I don't need a surname.

419
00:29:11,124 --> 00:29:12,375
I'm no samurai.

420
00:29:13,877 --> 00:29:15,336
You're one of my braves too.

421
00:29:16,254 --> 00:29:21,634
Even if it's for money, you're willing
to use your skills to help us.

422
00:29:24,304 --> 00:29:26,306
A ninja who serves no lord

423
00:29:27,098 --> 00:29:28,933
is just a thief.

424
00:29:29,017 --> 00:29:31,186
USE YOUR POWER FOR THE GOOD OF ALL
HAKUUNSAI

425
00:29:32,604 --> 00:29:33,813
Sarutobi…

426
00:29:36,065 --> 00:29:37,192
Sasuke.

427
00:29:41,446 --> 00:29:42,489
Don't need it.

428
00:29:47,702 --> 00:29:50,914
This Sanada cord marks us as comrades.

429
00:29:52,457 --> 00:29:53,750
Wear it proudly.

430
00:30:07,263 --> 00:30:09,015
Everyone, we're leaving the village.

431
00:30:23,780 --> 00:30:25,824
I'll now explain

432
00:30:26,783 --> 00:30:27,700
our escape plan.

433
00:30:39,546 --> 00:30:40,505
Come on!

434
00:30:42,757 --> 00:30:43,800
You got me!

435
00:30:44,509 --> 00:30:47,846
-As expected of a Tokugawa samurai.
-All right, one more round!

436
00:30:47,929 --> 00:30:50,306
-No, no. That's enough for today.
-Why?

437
00:30:50,390 --> 00:30:52,100
I've had a bit too much to drink.

438
00:30:52,809 --> 00:30:53,643
Careful!

439
00:30:53,726 --> 00:30:55,353
First, Nezu will steal the key

440
00:30:55,436 --> 00:30:57,397
to the village-facing gate
from the head clerk.

441
00:30:58,481 --> 00:30:59,899
Can you pull that off?

442
00:30:59,983 --> 00:31:03,111
We're all gambling buddies now.
I can swipe it anytime.

443
00:31:03,194 --> 00:31:06,281
By the way, Nezu can use
pretty much every ninja technique.

444
00:31:06,364 --> 00:31:08,116
He's just okay at all of them.

445
00:31:08,199 --> 00:31:09,325
Oh, come on.

446
00:31:09,409 --> 00:31:13,621
Once Nezu gets the key,
we'll use it to open the checkpoint gate.

447
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:15,582
But first, Sasuke…

448
00:31:29,262 --> 00:31:30,221
He flew!

449
00:31:32,140 --> 00:31:33,266
Amazing…

450
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:37,270
That's exactly…
the final piece our lord was waiting for.

451
00:31:42,609 --> 00:31:43,484
Yo.

452
00:32:00,543 --> 00:32:07,216
L-O-V-E U.

453
00:32:07,300 --> 00:32:08,551
Just kidding!

454
00:32:09,135 --> 00:32:10,470
That little punk…

455
00:32:11,763 --> 00:32:12,680
Let's go.

456
00:32:34,118 --> 00:32:34,994
All right.

457
00:33:19,163 --> 00:33:20,039
Good.

458
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:22,375
Now it's up to the old man.

459
00:33:26,963 --> 00:33:28,006
The gate's open.

460
00:33:29,215 --> 00:33:30,508
Mochizuki.

461
00:33:30,591 --> 00:33:31,968
-I'm counting on you.
-Yes, sir.

462
00:33:50,445 --> 00:33:51,362
Unno…

463
00:33:52,238 --> 00:33:53,948
lend us your strength.

464
00:34:05,543 --> 00:34:07,503
Come on, old man.

465
00:34:16,596 --> 00:34:17,972
Excuse me.

466
00:34:19,015 --> 00:34:20,349
What is it?

467
00:34:20,433 --> 00:34:23,227
We heard a suspicious noise.
I'll have it checked, just in case.

468
00:34:28,066 --> 00:34:29,442
What about the scout ninja?

469
00:34:31,486 --> 00:34:32,695
What's going on?

470
00:34:35,406 --> 00:34:37,784
This is bad. The guards are coming out.

471
00:34:37,867 --> 00:34:40,286
Stay calm. Trust Seikai.

472
00:34:45,124 --> 00:34:47,085
What's going on at this hour?

473
00:34:47,168 --> 00:34:49,045
Apparently, there was a suspicious noise.

474
00:34:51,547 --> 00:34:52,465
Who's there?

475
00:34:53,674 --> 00:34:55,426
You must all be exhausted.

476
00:34:57,553 --> 00:34:59,514
Spiritual Medicine,
Dream of the Butterfly.

477
00:35:02,350 --> 00:35:03,768
What is this…

478
00:35:08,189 --> 00:35:10,274
You'll be sleeping for a long, long time.

479
00:35:14,028 --> 00:35:14,946
Hey.

480
00:35:15,988 --> 00:35:18,032
What are you doing?!

481
00:35:18,116 --> 00:35:20,201
You fool! Hey.

482
00:35:21,661 --> 00:35:22,870
Scout ninja!

483
00:35:28,876 --> 00:35:29,710
And…

484
00:35:30,545 --> 00:35:31,420
who are you?

485
00:35:32,755 --> 00:35:34,215
Shakespeare said,

486
00:35:34,757 --> 00:35:40,513
"Fate carries your soul
to the place where it belongs most."

487
00:35:45,309 --> 00:35:47,770
Can I help you with something?

488
00:35:49,355 --> 00:35:50,648
-There's no next time.
-I know.

489
00:35:50,731 --> 00:35:52,608
-This is the last…
-Just shut up.

490
00:35:56,737 --> 00:35:57,864
Sasuke?

491
00:36:00,408 --> 00:36:01,742
Someone's beside him.

492
00:36:03,244 --> 00:36:04,245
That's…

493
00:36:07,832 --> 00:36:09,375
the Westerner from before.

494
00:36:12,503 --> 00:36:15,006
So he's going to break the lock
with a firearm.

495
00:36:22,930 --> 00:36:24,849
Looks like he got the message.

496
00:36:26,601 --> 00:36:28,561
So, what's your name?

497
00:36:29,687 --> 00:36:30,688
Cain Jude.

498
00:36:32,398 --> 00:36:33,691
Kakei Juzo?

499
00:36:34,358 --> 00:36:35,359
Cain…

500
00:36:38,154 --> 00:36:39,238
That'll do.

501
00:36:41,657 --> 00:36:43,284
Why did you come to help us?

502
00:36:44,327 --> 00:36:45,953
I repay my debts.

503
00:36:47,997 --> 00:36:49,874
You helped my comrades.

504
00:37:00,676 --> 00:37:03,346
You mean the fake blonde beauty?

505
00:37:06,098 --> 00:37:08,309
There are good ninja out there after all.

506
00:37:12,563 --> 00:37:14,065
What should we do, Lord Yukimura?

507
00:37:14,148 --> 00:37:16,234
If we use firearms,
the gunshot will give us away.

508
00:37:16,317 --> 00:37:18,152
The enemy will know for sure!

509
00:37:18,236 --> 00:37:20,780
We could take our chances
and run when the gun goes off.

510
00:37:39,799 --> 00:37:41,926
Raise the alarm! It's an emergency!

511
00:37:54,188 --> 00:37:55,064
The festival…

512
00:38:00,486 --> 00:38:03,030
This should mask the gunshot.

513
00:38:11,497 --> 00:38:12,540
Lucky us.

514
00:38:15,501 --> 00:38:17,295
-The lock's undone!
-So is the bolt!

515
00:38:17,378 --> 00:38:19,630
-How come?
-Let's just get going.

516
00:38:19,714 --> 00:38:20,715
Right!

517
00:38:30,433 --> 00:38:32,476
What's that sound?

518
00:38:35,563 --> 00:38:36,605
Lord Shuto!

519
00:38:38,316 --> 00:38:39,775
What's with the festival music?

520
00:38:39,859 --> 00:38:40,943
What's going on?

521
00:38:41,986 --> 00:38:43,070
Leave this to me.

522
00:38:44,155 --> 00:38:46,073
Go check on the village.

523
00:38:46,157 --> 00:38:47,158
Yes, sir!

524
00:38:47,241 --> 00:38:48,284
-Let's go.
-Right!

525
00:39:30,993 --> 00:39:32,286
All right.

526
00:39:53,974 --> 00:39:55,101
We did it!

527
00:40:06,779 --> 00:40:07,696
Let's go.

528
00:40:11,075 --> 00:40:11,992
Sasuke?

529
00:40:13,119 --> 00:40:14,078
Okuni.

530
00:40:14,161 --> 00:40:16,163
Are you heading to Osaka?

531
00:40:16,247 --> 00:40:17,248
Yeah.

532
00:40:17,331 --> 00:40:18,707
Here.

533
00:40:18,791 --> 00:40:20,418
I wove this with all my heart.

534
00:40:20,501 --> 00:40:22,670
I'm sure it'll protect you, Sasuke.

535
00:40:24,463 --> 00:40:25,840
-Thank you.
-Of course.

536
00:40:30,428 --> 00:40:31,345
Let's hurry!

537
00:40:31,929 --> 00:40:32,847
All right!

538
00:40:33,806 --> 00:40:34,849
-We did it.
-Yeah.

539
00:40:34,932 --> 00:40:36,809
Damn you, Sanada Yukimura!

540
00:40:38,060 --> 00:40:39,270
You won't get away!

541
00:40:40,271 --> 00:40:42,690
Sanada!

542
00:40:47,945 --> 00:40:49,363
What are they doing?

543
00:40:58,038 --> 00:41:00,791
At least let my grandchildren

544
00:41:01,792 --> 00:41:04,462
live in a world where hard work

545
00:41:04,545 --> 00:41:06,881
earns people enough to eat!

546
00:41:08,299 --> 00:41:09,467
Village headman…

547
00:41:11,218 --> 00:41:12,678
I'm counting on you!

548
00:41:12,761 --> 00:41:13,762
Did you…

549
00:41:14,263 --> 00:41:17,099
play that festival music
to help him escape?

550
00:41:17,183 --> 00:41:18,225
Shinkichi!

551
00:41:29,987 --> 00:41:32,323
Stay away!

552
00:41:34,992 --> 00:41:37,912
Sanada Yukimura…

553
00:41:41,749 --> 00:41:46,587
Go!

554
00:42:01,227 --> 00:42:02,228
Let's go.

555
00:42:28,963 --> 00:42:29,964
Too bad.

556
00:42:31,590 --> 00:42:35,636
Old man Yukimura's already long gone.

557
00:42:37,054 --> 00:42:38,347
I don't recognize you.

558
00:42:40,641 --> 00:42:41,725
Who are you?

559
00:42:49,233 --> 00:42:51,860
The peerless flying ninja…

560
00:42:54,863 --> 00:42:55,948
Sasuke.

561
00:42:57,533 --> 00:42:58,534
No.

562
00:43:01,287 --> 00:43:02,580
Sarutobi…

563
00:43:04,164 --> 00:43:05,791
Sasuke!

564
00:43:08,085 --> 00:43:09,753
Feel the weight of the lives…

565
00:43:13,549 --> 00:43:14,967
you've taken!

566
00:44:09,688 --> 00:44:12,566
I'm hungover…

567
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:16,153
and pissed off!

568
00:44:21,450 --> 00:44:24,078
Dual Barrage of the Eight Drunks.

569
00:44:24,161 --> 00:44:25,496
DUAL BARRAGE OF THE EIGHT DRUNKS

570
00:44:51,939 --> 00:44:53,107
Amazing…

571
00:44:56,068 --> 00:44:57,736
I smell blood.

572
00:45:12,709 --> 00:45:14,211
Die!

573
00:45:20,759 --> 00:45:21,844
Rising Serpent…

574
00:45:22,761 --> 00:45:24,179
Sickle Weasel!

575
00:45:42,865 --> 00:45:46,493
Thanks for everything these past 14 years.

576
00:45:52,207 --> 00:45:54,001
You're all together.

577
00:45:55,586 --> 00:45:57,254
You won't be lonely.

578
00:46:02,176 --> 00:46:03,677
Damn Shuto.

579
00:46:04,636 --> 00:46:06,430
He let them get away.

580
00:46:09,016 --> 00:46:10,642
Where are they headed?

581
00:46:11,935 --> 00:46:12,811
Apparently…

582
00:46:13,645 --> 00:46:14,480
Osaka.

583
00:46:16,482 --> 00:46:17,649
South, huh?

584
00:46:17,733 --> 00:46:19,234
No, north.

585
00:46:28,911 --> 00:46:30,913
Subtitle translation by: Sayo Takada

586
00:46:30,996 --> 00:46:32,915
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
